From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:54:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: reject a TWT agreement with no sleep time

mt7915_mac_check_twt_req() refused a wake interval shorter than the
minimum wake duration, but accepted one exactly as long. The station
is then awake for the whole interval and never sleeps, which gains
nothing; such a schedule was reported to stall tx on the MT7915 family.

Refuse an interval no longer than the wake duration.
mt7915_test_twt_interval checks both sides of the boundary.

Ported from pesa1234/openwrt next-r4.12.0.rss.mtk,
6014-mt7915-reject-TWT-with-zero-sleep-duration (Erik Karlsson).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c            | 3 ++-
 mt7915/tests/mac-test.c | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 8436dbf1..4b6bff33 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -2374,8 +2374,9 @@ static int mt7915_mac_check_twt_req(struct ieee80211_twt_setup *twt)
 	mantissa = le16_to_cpu(twt_agrt->mantissa);
 	duration = twt_agrt->min_twt_dur << 8;
 
+	/* a station awake for its whole interval never sleeps */
 	interval = (u64)mantissa << exp;
-	if (!interval || interval < duration)
+	if (!interval || interval <= duration)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	return 0;
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
index bd065b90..a6325325 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@ static int mt7915_test_twt_check(u16 mantissa, u8 exp, u8 min_dur)
 	return mt7915_mac_check_twt_req(setup);
 }
 
-/* A station can't set up an agreement with a zero wake interval. */
+/* A station can't set up an agreement with a zero wake interval, or one
+ * it would spend awake.
+ */
 static void mt7915_test_twt_interval(struct kunit *test)
 {
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(0, 0, 0), -EOPNOTSUPP);
@@ -44,6 +46,9 @@ static void mt7915_test_twt_interval(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(1024, 10, 4), 0);
 	/* interval shorter than the minimum wake duration */
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(1, 0, 4), -EOPNOTSUPP);
+	/* as long as it (4 * 256 us): no sleep; 1 us longer is fine */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(1024, 0, 4), -EOPNOTSUPP);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(1025, 0, 4), 0);
 	/* intervals beyond 32 bits are valid requests */
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_twt_check(2, 31, 4), 0);
 }
